# Quests: generated by tools/quests/make_quests.py, edit there
betterquesting.questline.7dZOq4U1Vfa2Yr9apUvsiQ.name=Better Communications
betterquesting.questline.7dZOq4U1Vfa2Yr9apUvsiQ.desc=Telephones on pylon lines, radios, mobile phones and satellites, carried by voice chat.
betterquesting.quest.IHTr1EMRVx6vQQ7722eirw.name=§2§lWired for Sound
betterquesting.quest.IHTr1EMRVx6vQQ7722eirw.desc=Every phone network starts with a wire. Phone Cable is red alloy wire wrapped in rubber, and you make it in the Assembler.%n%nIt runs from a Telephone to its Line Terminal, up to 32 blocks of it, and the signal loses nothing on the way. Make a couple to get started.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:wired.md]The wired network[/guide].
betterquesting.quest.b14IecXxXxuWU8oeGOPcNw.name=§2§lRing, Ring
betterquesting.quest.b14IecXxXxuWU8oeGOPcNw.desc=A circuit, a note block for the bell and a steel body, put together in the Assembler with a cord of Phone Cable: that's a Telephone.%n%nRight-click it to pick up the handset. It's yours, and so is its six-digit number.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:wired.md]The wired network[/guide].
betterquesting.quest.mXRjCMiFWsyGTG0Id2bbig.name=§2§lEnd of the Line
betterquesting.quest.mXRjCMiFWsyGTG0Id2bbig.desc=Every line starts and ends at a Line Terminal. Give it LV power, just 4 EU/t, and run Phone Cable from it to a Telephone. A terminal serves exactly one phone.%n%nTo put it on a line, wrench the terminal, then a Pylon Head.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:wired.md]The wired network[/guide].
betterquesting.quest._OpArmItVHW8jB5_z18yig.name=§2§lUp on the Pole
betterquesting.quest._OpArmItVHW8jB5_z18yig.desc=Phone Cable only reaches 32 blocks. For anything farther, put up pylons: a Pylon Head on top of a pole of 6 to 16 Wood Frame Boxes, with a crossarm of 4 more right under the head.%n%nTaller is better. Two pylons link up to four times the shorter one's height apart, if nothing solid is in between. Wrench one head, then the other, to link them.%n%nPylons need no power and keep working in unloaded chunks. The signal still fades with distance, so you'll want a repeater at least every 225 blocks.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:wired.md]The wired network[/guide].
betterquesting.quest._xekW5q3V6-D2yESxW4Bqw.name=§2§lHello? Can You Hear Me?
betterquesting.quest._xekW5q3V6-D2yESxW4Bqw.desc=Time for your first call! You need two Telephones, each on its own Line Terminal, with pylons between the terminals.%n%nPick up the handset. If there's only one other phone on the line, it rings right away. Otherwise, dial its number or pick a contact.%n%nDon't expect hi-fi: a Telephone sounds narrow and gritty. But it carries your voice as far as the line goes.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:wired.md]The wired network[/guide].
betterquesting.quest.EwUn7B5YXiqaZtu5vTGc2Q.name=§2§lKeeping the Signal Alive
betterquesting.quest.EwUn7B5YXiqaZtu5vTGc2Q.desc=Long lines get quiet. A Repeater Head is a Pylon Head that cleans up the signal, so line loss starts over after it.%n%nUnlike a plain pylon it needs power: 4 EU/t of LV, through an Energy Hatch in a cabinet at the pole's foot. It only works while it's loaded and powered, so keep your repeaters chunkloaded.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:wired.md]The wired network[/guide].
betterquesting.quest.ARn2PctkVOe0cqI7997r1Q.name=§2§lSwitchboard
betterquesting.quest.ARn2PctkVOe0cqI7997r1Q.desc=A plain line joins exactly two phones. Want more? A Router Head has 15 link slots and turns your lines into a network, where any phone can dial any other.%n%nIt cleans up the signal like a repeater, and takes 16 EU/t of LV power through an Energy Hatch in the exchange cabinet at the pole's foot: three across, two high, with a second crossarm up top for all those lines.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:wired.md]The wired network[/guide].
betterquesting.quest.UYdKN4lyUKWOiqsyX6luCQ.name=§2§lOn the Air
betterquesting.quest.UYdKN4lyUKWOiqsyX6luCQ.desc=Time to cut the cord. An Antenna T1 Head tops a guyed mast of 6 to 32 Steel Frame Boxes, a dipole under the head and three guys down to LV Machine Casing anchors; its Energy Hatch goes in the equipment shelter in front. It uses 32 EU/t.%n%nIt reaches about 64 blocks on open ground. Height helps; hills and roofs cost you signal. Antennas find each other on their own, and wrenching one to a Pylon Head or Line Terminal within 16 blocks carries that line over the air.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:antennas.md]Antennas[/guide].
betterquesting.quest.VdecT0iBUsCxBEbIo6xNeA.name=§6§lBase Station
betterquesting.quest.VdecT0iBUsCxBEbIo6xNeA.desc=A Transceiver is a radio in a block. It runs on MV, 32 EU/t, and reaches about 125 blocks on open ground on its own.%n%nStand within 2 blocks of it and hold the radio push-to-talk key (Caps Lock, unless you changed it) to talk on its channel. Its loudspeaker plays the channel to everyone within 16 blocks.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:radios.md]Radios[/guide].
betterquesting.quest.8sQY72VCXU2ZURqIKp1zVw.name=§6§lReading the Air
betterquesting.quest.8sQY72VCXU2ZURqIKp1zVw.desc=Radio is fussy, and the Signal Analyzer tells you why. Hold it to see your signal: its strength in dB, its level, the antenna serving you, and what's costing you the most, be it distance, terrain, cover, weather or noise.%n%nA link needs 6 dB for Low and 12 for Medium. Below 4 dB it cuts out at once; between 4 and 6 it holds for 3 seconds, then drops.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:analyzer.md]The Signal Analyzer[/guide].
betterquesting.quest.82uwmy_wU3eMPoGqyurVlw.name=§6§lPocket Radio
betterquesting.quest.82uwmy_wU3eMPoGqyurVlw.desc=A radio you can carry. The Walkie-Talkie runs on its own MV battery; charge it like any GT tool.%n%nRight-click to pick one of 16 channels or switch it off, or sneak and scroll to change channel. Hold push-to-talk to transmit. It reaches about 80 blocks on its own, and much farther through antennas.%n%nAnyone within 6 blocks hears what it receives, so it's no good for secrets.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:radios.md]Radios[/guide].
betterquesting.quest.gNOxxRElWUebInHOkYOeQw.name=§6§lOver and Out
betterquesting.quest.gNOxxRElWUebInHOkYOeQw.desc=Now put it to use! Talk to someone over the radio, or hear them: on a walkie, through a Transceiver, or through the antennas between you. It has to go over the radio: hearing them in person doesn't count.%n%nRadio etiquette: channels are open to anyone tuned in, and when two people talk at once, each listener only hears the stronger one. Say "over" when you're done.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:radios.md]Radios[/guide].
betterquesting.quest.BRsUHvwqVhSei0mx4y1eWg.name=§6§lA Taller Mast
betterquesting.quest.BRsUHvwqVhSei0mx4y1eWg.desc=Same idea, more reach. An Antenna T2 Head tops a taller guyed mast of Aluminium Frame Boxes, 8 to 32 of them, with two crossed dipoles and MV Machine Casings, and uses 128 EU/t.%n%nIt reaches about 128 blocks, twice a T1: every 6 dB of link budget doubles the range on open ground. Antennas repeat all 16 radio channels between them, and carry calls between the lines bridged onto them.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:antennas.md]Antennas[/guide].
betterquesting.quest.fia8emGdXIqzunSxVhLBng.name=§5§lAcross the Valley
betterquesting.quest.fia8emGdXIqzunSxVhLBng.desc=An Antenna T3 Head tops a self-supporting lattice tower of Stainless Steel Frame Boxes on HV Machine Casings, panel antennas round its top, uses 512 EU/t and reaches about 256 blocks.%n%nBuild it high. It surveys the land around it every five minutes, and a hill in the way can cost you more than the distance does.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:antennas.md]Antennas[/guide].
betterquesting.quest.Cs4eUVpnUBeevZzOvcInrw.name=§6§lFace to Face
betterquesting.quest.Cs4eUVpnUBeevZzOvcInrw.desc=A speakerphone with a screen, for the whole team. The Videophone runs on MV, 32 EU/t, and connects to a Line Terminal with Phone Cable, just like a Telephone.%n%nRight-click it to dial, answer or hang up. Everyone within 4 blocks is in the call and on screen, and its loudspeaker carries the call 16 blocks. It hangs up by itself 30 seconds after the last person walks away.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:phones.md]Phones[/guide].
betterquesting.quest.1e_b8ZF0VRq1STROZstNIg.name=§6§lSeeing Is Believing
betterquesting.quest.1e_b8ZF0VRq1STROZstNIg.desc=See someone in a video call, on a Videophone, a Mobile Phone or an ME Phone, with their front camera on.%n%nThe front camera shows your character; the rear camera shows what you see, in calls of two at High or better. Video needs at least Medium: at Low the picture freezes, but the voice carries on.%n%nThe phone screen's Video tab shows the call full size and switches each camera on or off.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:phones.md]Phones[/guide].
betterquesting.quest.tmuzvF6QVE-ZigvcfAhM5Q.name=§5§lPhone in Your Pocket
betterquesting.quest.tmuzvF6QVE-ZigvcfAhM5Q.desc=A phone that goes where you go. The Mobile Phone gets its service from antennas: about 64 blocks from a T1 on open ground, twice that from a T2.%n%nIt gets its number the first time you use it, and works from your inventory or a bauble slot. The Phone key (N, unless you changed it) answers, hangs up, or opens its screen.%n%nIts battery holds 1,200,000 EU and drains 4 EU/t on standby, 16 in a call.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:phones.md]Phones[/guide].
betterquesting.quest.QTf-qLjuX5uncRhFsloOcg.name=§5§lCan You Hear Me Now?
betterquesting.quest.QTf-qLjuX5uncRhFsloOcg.desc=Make or take a call on a Mobile Phone. Hold it to see your bars.%n%nBad weather hurts: rain costs a phone 3 dB of service, a thunderstorm 6. Not sure where you have coverage? An antenna's screen maps where its signal reaches.%n%nIn a call, add more phones from the keypad: up to 8 people can talk together.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:phones.md]Phones[/guide].
betterquesting.quest.SSBYl-CuVHeaS00Zgy5NWA.name=§8§lWireless Everywhere
betterquesting.quest.SSBYl-CuVHeaS00Zgy5NWA.desc=Got an ME network with wireless access points? Then you already have coverage. An ME Phone is a Mobile Phone linked to an ME network.%n%nLink it at a Security Terminal, like a Wireless Terminal. Wherever that network's access points reach, boosters included, it has service at Max. It charges in an AE2 Charger.%n%nME Phones on the same ME network call each other with no antenna at all.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:phones.md]Phones[/guide].
betterquesting.quest.6JNs0PJ2W_2dWPcb8B5q0A.name=§8§lBridging the Networks
betterquesting.quest.6JNs0PJ2W_2dWPcb8B5q0A.desc=An ME Bridge joins an ME network to your phone network, so ME Phones can call any phone.%n%nPut it on ME cable, where it takes one channel, and wrench-link it to a Pylon Head, a Line Terminal or an antenna within 16 blocks. It uses 512 EU/t.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:phones.md]Phones[/guide].
betterquesting.quest.1FYiW9xFV5eNdWDcFL6cbw.name=§8§lLong Distance
betterquesting.quest.1FYiW9xFV5eNdWDcFL6cbw.desc=Your ME Phone can reach past your ME network. From an ME Phone, call a Telephone on a line, a Mobile Phone or a Videophone, through an ME Bridge.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:phones.md]Phones[/guide].
betterquesting.quest.oNm-cIc3Xoy6hejGu6UM7Q.name=§6§lThrough the Portal
betterquesting.quest.oNm-cIc3Xoy6hejGu6UM7Q.desc=Radio doesn't cross dimensions on its own. A Portal Relay works within 4 blocks of a Nether portal, an End portal, a Twilight Forest portal or a Personal Space portal, on 32 EU/t of MV power.%n%nWrench-link it to an antenna, a Pylon Head or a Line Terminal of your network. Then wrench the relay, go through the portal, and wrench a relay on the other side within 5 minutes. The pair joins the two networks at High.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:space.md]Space and other dimensions[/guide].
betterquesting.quest.78j3bHKHWF6_v27ljQ8cYg.name=§5§lPayload
betterquesting.quest.78j3bHKHWF6_v27ljQ8cYg.desc=A Satellite is an HV emitter and sensor with two solar panels. Put it on Galacticraft's Tier 1 rocket parts in the Assembler, and you've got a Satellite Rocket.%n%nDon't bother with Galacticraft's launch pads: this rocket only flies from a Satellite Launch Pad.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:space.md]Space and other dimensions[/guide].
betterquesting.quest.CW6Vyi4yXYClMf9my2HQKQ.name=§5§lLiftoff
betterquesting.quest.CW6Vyi4yXYClMf9my2HQKQ.desc=3, 2, 1... The Satellite Launch Pad is a whole launch complex: a pad of Clean Stainless Steel Machine Casings round a flame pit, a service tower behind it with an Input Bus for rockets in its base, a propellant tank with an Input Hatch for rocket fuel, lightning masts, and an Energy Hatch and a Maintenance Hatch on the pad's front edge. Keep the sky open over the pit.%n%nA launch takes 30 seconds at 480 EU/t and 1,000 L of fuel, and puts a satellite into orbit over the pad's dimension. Build the pad and watch your first satellite go up.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:space.md]Space and other dimensions[/guide].
betterquesting.quest.J3UFmY7aUkyD5jAJI7lDBw.name=§5§lA Constellation
betterquesting.quest.J3UFmY7aUkyD5jAJI7lDBw.desc=One satellite gets lonely. Put 5 over a dimension and every phone and radio under its open sky gets a signal from them, at Low. 14 give Medium, 37 High and 100 Max.%n%nA roof weakens the signal, and rain costs a few dB. Satellites come down after about 100 days, so keep launching.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:space.md]Space and other dimensions[/guide].
betterquesting.quest.aEl8W97yVGeFRBy0p4O4ZA.name=§5§lDish Network
betterquesting.quest.aEl8W97yVGeFRBy0p4O4ZA.desc=Why run lines when you can bounce off a satellite? A Satellite Dish joins its network to every other dish in the same dimension, through the satellites overhead.%n%nIt's a bowl of Clean Stainless Steel Machine Casings facing the sky, a feed horn on four struts over it, on a pedestal of Stainless Steel Frame Boxes; the Energy Hatch and Maintenance Hatch go in the plinth at its foot, by the controller. It uses 512 EU/t.%n%nWrench-link it to an antenna, a Pylon Head or a Line Terminal. Keep up its maintenance: each problem costs it 2 dB.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:space.md]Space and other dimensions[/guide].
betterquesting.quest.iphLiVwwUKakj8QR4PH2-w.name=§5§lCalling Home
betterquesting.quest.iphLiVwwUKakj8QR4PH2-w.desc=Your rocket is parked on another planet. Why not make it useful? Put a Rocket Radio Receiver in its cargo while it stands on a launch pad, and the rocket becomes an antenna there, linked to the Overworld's satellites at High.%n%nThe rocket needs chests to have cargo. Back in the Overworld, phones under open sky and networks with a dish can reach it.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:space.md]Space and other dimensions[/guide].
betterquesting.quest.Ww6rBsobWMmbyc-M1rYILg.name=§5§lOut of This World
betterquesting.quest.Ww6rBsobWMmbyc-M1rYILg.desc=Call someone in another dimension: through a pair of Portal Relays to the Nether, the End, the Twilight Forest or a personal dimension, or through the Overworld's satellites to a planet with a Rocket Radio Receiver.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:space.md]Space and other dimensions[/guide].
